v 3
d stexcess: fit excess hazard models with a modelled reference rate
d
d Modelled excess hazard models: a relative-survival / excess-hazard
d model in which the expected (reference) rate is itself a fitted
d hazard model estimated from a control cohort, rather than taken
d from external population life tables. Pure Stata/Mata
d implementation with exact analytic derivatives; supports multiple
d timescales, time-varying effects, two-stage estimation and
d regression-standardised predictions with delta-method CIs.
d
d Requires Stata 19.5 or later.
d
d Author: Michael J. Crowther, Red Door Analytics AB
d Support: michael.crowther@reddooranalytics.se
d
d Distribution-Date: 20260611
f ado/stexcess.ado
f ado/stexcess_p.ado
f ado/lstexcess.mlib
f help/stexcess.sthlp
f help/stexcess_postestimation.sthlp
f data/stexcess_example.dta
